# GLM-5.2-MXFP4 decode perf-opt (gfx950 / MI355X)

## Profile (2026-07-01)
`utilities/glm52_decode_prof_0701.csv` — GLM-5.2 decode, in1024/out1024, conc4, TP0,
graph-ON Σdur; MI355X mxfp4 vs B200 nvfp4.

CAVEAT: this MI355X run did NOT use our faster Triton DSA prefill/indexer kernel
(`SGLANG_DSA_TRITON_PREFILL`) — it is the stock tilelang/aiter indexer path, so the
indexer gaps below are an UPPER bound (not reprofiling; build against these gaps).

Per-forward Σdur (3 dense A-layers + 75 MoE B-layers): MI355X 15,153us vs B200
11,742us (B200 = 77%, MI355X ~1.29x slower). Overlap: MI355X 1.00x vs B200 1.33x
(structural — wall-clock/TPOT loses further).

Section gap (×75 MoE layers; ratio = B200/MI355X, lower = MI355X slower):

| Section | MI355X us | B200 us | ratio | overall opportunity |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| DeepseekV2AttentionMLA | 6588 | 4242 | 64% | 15.5%  (BIGGEST) |
| DeepseekV2MoE | 6234 | 5912 | 95% | 2.1%  (parity, SKIP) |
| prepare_mlp (AllReduce) | 1285 | 575 | 45% | 4.7% |
| prepare_attn | 371 | 575 | 155% | MI355X already faster |

MoE is at PARITY. The gap is ATTENTION + AllReduce.

Inside attention: the core sparse-MLA `main_kernel` (9.22us) is ON PAR with B200
`fmhaSm100fKernel` (9.52us) — NOT the problem. The MI355X cost is the DSA Indexer's
many small UNFUSED kernels that B200 fuses (its RopeQuantizeKernel does rope+quant
in 2.89us):
- Indexer RotaryEmbedding 9.16us vs 2.16us  (4.2x slower)  <- worst single item
- Indexer LayerNorm       5.51us vs 1.83us  (3x)
- separate: act_quant 5.78, indexer_k_quant_and_cache 5.80, hadamard 4.81,
  topk_transform 5.78, _get_logits_head_gate gemm 6.83 + mul 5.47
- RowParallelLinear 12.85us  (large bf16 GEMM, likely untuned)
- prepare_mlp AllReduce cross_device_reduce_1stage 12.18us vs trtllm 7.67us

## ROOT CAUSE of the indexer gap (2026-07-03)
The fused indexer kernels (`fused_q_indexer_rope_first_quant`,
`fused_k_indexer_norm_rope`, `fused_k_indexer_norm_rope_store` from
`sglang.jit_kernel.dsv4`/`dsv32`) are gated behind `if _is_cuda:`
(dsa_indexer.py:153) — NVIDIA-only. On HIP/gfx950 they never import, so the
indexer runs UNFUSED (_get_q_k_bf16 -> separate rotary_emb@602 + layernorm +
quant + store), which is exactly the profile's fragmented kernels. B200 fuses
them (RopeQuantizeKernel 2.89us) -> the ~1.5x indexer gap.
Standalone fused-rope was tried TWICE and reverted e2e-neutral (586aff9350,
5c5288dfe5) — the win is the MEGA-fusion (rope+quant+store), not rope alone.
The HIP megafusion already exists: aiter `indexer_qk_rope_quant_and_cache`
behind `SGLANG_DSA_FUSE_INDEXER_QK` (built+validated byte-exact+GSM8K earlier),
UNWIRED from decode because it was e2e-neutral on GLM-5.1's COLLECTIVE-bound
decode. GLM-5.2 profile shows the indexer is now the RAW gap -> revisit here.

## DIRECTION (2026-07-03): fix the SLOW PRIMITIVES, not fusion.
Fusing slow kernels just bundles the slowness. The indexer's individual ops are
themselves 3-4x slower than B200 on tiny work -> kernel inefficiency
(launch/occupancy or the aiter indirect cached-position gather), not fusion
overhead. Fix these first:
- Indexer RotaryEmbedding: aiter kn_entry_2c_sbhd_cached_indirect_inplace 9.16us
  vs B200 fused_rope 2.16us (4.2x). Tiny work (16 heads x 64 rope dims) -> absurd.
- Indexer LayerNorm: ck_tile Layernorm2dFwd 5.51us vs B200 1.83us (3x). 128-dim.

